TEXT 0 -224 Left 2 ;First-order high-pass (CR): H(s) = sRC / (1 + sRC) = s / (s + ωc)\nfc = 1 / (2π RC) ≈ 1.59 kHz: one pole at s = −1/RC and a zero at s = 0.\nStep: out jumps to 1 and decays as e^(−t/τ). Bode: +20 dB/decade below fc and flat above; the phase goes from +90° to 0.
